  "description": "Sounds of a family of free-ranging capuchin monkeys in the Atlantic Rainforest. The vocalizations of the animals and their movement through the trees are audible. The sounds of various birds can also be heard. This audio recording, captured in mono, can be used for the training of artificial intelligence and bioacoustics algorithms. Atlantic Rainforest Biome\n- Recording date: March 23, 2025 - 11:30 AM. Early autumn\n- Recorder: Zoom, model H1N.\n- Microphone: Superlux, model ECM888B - The measurement microphone was attached to a horn-type sound concentrator that I designed and 3D printed, thus recording distant sounds in the forest.\n- Garuva, State of Santa Catarina, Brazil\nCitation: ARAUJO, R. L., A wild family of Capuchin Monkeys in the Atlantic Rainforest,  Itapoá, Brazil. Freesound link: www.....",
